{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/design/dao.star.md | tail -12'","aggregated_output":"   151\t## Deferred\n   152\t\n   153\t- **Multi-shot forks** (Arc's back button resuming a sibling branch): branch identity and subscription routing with a non-unique current are unspecified.\n   154\t- **Local projection** in Mode 2: the browser `yin.vm` appends the same Datastar-format effects to a browser-local egress stream read by a browser-side boundary adapter; same vocabulary, different boundary.\n   155\t- **Compaction of the session-facts medium**: waits on `dao.stream.md` OD-4.\n   156\t- **The content service as rules**: `dao.jing.content` is a plan section, not a spec; the notice above depends on it.\n   157\t- **An HTTP channel for peers without WebSocket**: `dao.stream.http.md`, Deferred.\n   158\t\n   159\t## Completion Criteria\n   160\t\n   161\t1. **Thin Client**: A `yin.vm` agent receives a Datastar input through the HTTP boundary's ingress stream, answers with `:http/head`, SSE-formatted `:http/chunk`s and `:http/end` on the egress stream, parks, and resumes on the next input for its current token. Also: a request with no token begins a lineage; a subscribe consumes nothing and a re-subscribe after several inputs receives the current projection; a stale token is re-projected; a closed socket is observed as `:http/closed`; a silent exchange lapses and closes; a lineage nobody returns to lapses, its parked record is retired and its facts remain; a request naming a just-published token is never answered as begin; after an ingress gap no exchange is unleased, no closed exchange stays leased, and no driver renews one.\n   162\t2. **Fat Client Handoff**, conditional on UCF version 1 landing: a `yin.vm` agent exports under exclusive custody, the SSE patch carries the notice, a CLJS `yin.vm` in the browser fetches the body through the lineage's gated content pair, verifies it, obtains the grant, resumes, and reaches a server-held stream through a gated, leased reflection. Migration back from an allow-listed peer is admitted under *Admitting a continuation back*. The carrier shape is an architect ruling pending the owner's confirmation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
