{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The pass order closes the token race for direct local reads. It does not close it over reflections: a reflected `next` can return `blocked` while its source read is still pending, even after the source accepted the fact. The lease-gap fallback addresses the other concern: a driver that misses a lapse record drops all subscriptions on its own cursor’s `gap`, so it need not recover that record individually."}}
